# BROAD JUMP

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Broad Jump is an explosive lower-body exercise and assessment performed by projecting the body forward as far as possible from a standing position.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the most valuable assessments and developers of horizontal power.

---

# Philosophy

Combat athletes rarely express power purely vertically.

They accelerate.

Close distance.

Drive through opponents.

Shoot for takedowns.

Explode into combinations.

The Broad Jump develops and measures these qualities.

CAS uses the Broad Jump to improve horizontal explosiveness while monitoring lower-body power.

